Z||000000||Mach10||05-07-2001||11:30 PM||||I've had my 1st Fiero for just over 24hrs, and the head gasket on the rear head has just gone... ****  PISS ****!!!<P>Well, the heads are being taken apart and decked for this, so I was wondering if anyone had any ideas for some light mods to do to the heads while they're off.<P>I was thinking along the lines of a new valve job, springs, and some roller-tip rockers, since that'll be mostly cost of parts... Thoughts?||||reg||8
Z||000001||RedOktober||05-08-2001||02:04 AM||||I recommend porting the headers( Grinding the little flanges on the inside ir the headers) while they are off, as well as installing NEW header Studs or Bolts. <P>Also, clean out your intake manifolds all three pieces. Replace all the rubber lines and double check all of your vacuum lines to make sure they are not cracked or broken. <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrgone||05-08-2001||07:49 AM||||oh yeah? you wanna hear bad luck....<P>the day my fiero was dropped off at my house, i took it around the lot a bit and when i parked it it was smoking prefusley.<BR>just oil on the engine but i was scared for a good 12 hours.<P>after 1300$ repairs (rear inner tirods are expensive from the dealer) and i get plates and insurance, take the car out for 1 hour. 1 hour! and the gearshift comes loose from the linkage leaving the car stuck and me stranded<P>i get the car back today.<BR>im scared.||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||05-08-2001||08:00 AM||||Ya need to remove the bad carma from the previous owner. My 84 brokedown the first time I drove it to work. My wife suggested I look for items the previous owner left behind. I though yeah ok. a week later I fried my engine sooo I started looking sure enough I found a drivers license in the sun visor from the original owner (expire 85)along with a few mini disks, once I took them out every thing was fine and has been so far<P>I almost feel stupid for posting this but whatever works.<P>Outer Limits bah humbug||||reg||3
Z||000004||Taijiguy||05-08-2001||08:05 AM||||I agree about porting the heads. You can do it yourself, just use a die grinder, and a Dremel with a pencil adaptor. Do it before you have the valve job done. (just in case you run off into a valve seat or should burr up a valve guide) The only thing to be aware of, is the little sharks-fin that sticks up inside of the openings...don't grind it down, just smooth it up a little. It's not an obstruction, it actually improves flow. <BR>Also, instead of buying the roller rockers for the Fiero, which are pretty expensive comparitively, you can replace the studs with 3/8 or 5/16, and install SBC rollers. They sit about .030" off center of the valve stem, but that's plenty acceptable with rollers. This also gives you a wider variety of rockers and ratios to choose from. Also, enlarging the valve spring pockets some will allow the use of SBC valve springs.<BR>DOn't forget to remove the obstructions inside the exhaust manifold as mentioned before as well.<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrgone||05-08-2001||08:24 AM||||bad carma hmm..<P>i havent found any of that yet. although i have found some interesting ... uh 'repairs'<P>like the big peice of CHAIN and 8 muffler clamps holding my exhaust on<P>the bungee cord tight under the syspention pod? wrapped around the battery box, holding a huge battery in<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||05-08-2001||08:25 AM||||I'm reasonably sure that the Karma (Carma?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) problem lies with me. ****  like this ALWAYS happens to me. THat's why I got a Fiero. If the damn thing's going to break down on my, I should at least have fun with it!<BR>Maybe I'll sprinkle SeaSalt in the car. That'll neutralize any curses...<P>I'm definitely going to have the exhaust ported. Unfortunately, I don't have the time to have the heads done by myself, so I have to have the machine shop do it. ($$$) So, I have to keep the budget pretty low. I'm <P>thinking that a new valve set would be nice. I'm wanting to maybe put some higher-ratio rockers on to give me a little bump in performance. Nothing spectacular. <BR>All I'm asking for is Mid 11's in the 1/4 mile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I have heard really good things about roller-tips, but again, I'll be having someone else do this "While it's already apart" so I have to keep costs down. Also bear in mind that this engine will only be in this car for another year (cross fingers!) so just needs a LITTLE more boot.<P>Wish me luck!||||reg||6
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||05-08-2001||09:50 AM||||I had 2 days before the bad carma hit me. Drove the car home and arround for 2 days, the exhaust was kinda loud but on the second day when I stoped and let it idle, I heard a bit of a knocking noise. well, a rebuild later (including a new 3.1 crank and 5 new rods) she was back on the roads flying arround.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||05-08-2001||10:30 AM||||One of the reasons for all these sad stories is when someone owns a car for a few years they get very tuned-in to the sounds and the feel of the car.<P>and if it starts to act odd they will baby it.<P>and if they have a sense that something is going wrong, they might giveup on it and decide to sell it while its still running.<P>  but when you buy a used car, you dont have that aquired sense for it, you get in and push it hard, you wanna see what she will do.<P>  Sometimes thats all it takes to blow a head gasket, exhaust manifold, or throw a rod.<P>   I had a VW bug that I drove for a year with a chattering connecting rod. I babied it and didnt rev it up very high. I let a friend of mind drive it for 5 miles. He told me, "ya know your lugging this engine, its a four cylinder, you need to wind it up more before you upshift.<P>  Threw the rod right through the top of the crankcase.<P>  Never even apoligized!||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrgone||05-08-2001||04:50 PM||||called the shop, car needs a new shift rod...<BR>they temporarily epoxyed the clip to the broken one....      you think it will hold for a few days?||||reg||9
Z||000010||Dave Gunsul||05-08-2001||08:30 PM||||If you're going to put in a higher ratio rocker arm don't forget to put in performance springs too. (Crane or Comp. Cams.) A multi angle valve job will show the best results in porting for the street.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
